.SS "MASQUE on a forward listener"
.PP
HTTP \fBCONNECT\fR tunnels TCP, and that is all it tunnels. Everything else an estate sends \[u2014] DNS, QUIC, NTP, WireGuard, telemetry \[u2014] either leaves the network outside this policy or does not leave at all, and the first is the usual answer. CONNECT\-UDP (RFC 9298) is the same explicit proxy for datagrams, with the same destination rules, credentials, logs and bans; CONNECT\-IP (RFC 9484) carries IP packets, which is how a MASQUE VPN is built.
.PP
.TS
