.SS "upstreams[].hedge"
.PP
Hedging trades a little extra load for a shorter tail latency: if the request in flight has not answered within \fBdelay\fR, a copy goes to another endpoint, and whichever returns a usable response first wins while the others are cancelled. Only replayable requests (GET, HEAD, OPTIONS, TRACE without a body) are hedged, each copy is keyed to a distinct endpoint, and every copy beyond the first is gated by \fBretry_budget\fR when one is set.
