T}	T{
How long the client stays marked;\: at most 720h. An explicit \fB0s\fR marks nobody,\: which is what a decoy served honestly (\fBrobots\fR,\: \fBsitemap\fR) wants: reading it is what a crawler is meant to do,\: and asking for what it names is a different route
T}
.TE
.PP
The built\-in decoys, each a plausible page for the thing a scanner is looking for and each containing nothing an operator would mind being read \[u2014] every credential, key and host name in them is visibly fake, and a test refuses a decoy that hands out a password, a token or a key without a marker that says so:
