.SS "routes[].doh"
.PP
A \fBdoh\fR route answers DNS over HTTPS (RFC 8484) for clients: \fBGET\fR with the query in the \fBdns\fR parameter (base64url without padding) or \fBPOST\fR with an \fBapplication/dns\-message\fR body. The query goes through the named \fBkind: dns\fR listener\(aqs policy and cache (bans, client allow list, rate limit, block list) as if it had arrived over UDP, and the answer is returned as \fBapplication/dns\-message\fR with \fBCache\-Control: max\-age\fR set to the smallest TTL in it. A query the policy drops answers 403; bad requests 400, a wrong content type 415, other methods 405. The route\(aqs own admission pipeline (rate limits, ACLs, WAF) applies first, so a DoH endpoint can be limited like any other route.
.PP
.TS
