.SS "Kind \fBopenapi\fR"
.PP
Validates requests against an OpenAPI 3.0 or 3.1 description (JSON or YAML): the path must be documented (concrete paths win over templated ones), the method defined for it (else 405 with \fBAllow\fR), path, query, header and cookie parameters present when required and matching their schema (strings are coerced to the declared type), the content type one the operation declares (else 415) and a JSON body valid against its schema. The schema subset covers types and \fBnullable\fR, \fBenum\fR, \fBconst\fR, \fBrequired\fR, \fBproperties\fR, \fBadditionalProperties\fR, \fBpatternProperties\fR, \fBitems\fR, \fBminItems\fR/\fBmaxItems\fR/\fBuniqueItems\fR, \fBminLength\fR/\fBmaxLength\fR/ \fBpattern\fR, \fBminimum\fR/\fBmaximum\fR (exclusive too), \fBmultipleOf\fR, \fBminProperties\fR/\fBmaxProperties\fR, \fBallOf\fR/\fBanyOf\fR/\fBoneOf\fR/\fBnot\fR, local \fB$ref\fR and the formats \fBdate\-time\fR, \fBdate\fR, \fBemail\fR, \fBuuid\fR, \fBipv4\fR, \fBipv6\fR, \fBuri\fR and \fBhostname\fR; other keywords and formats are ignored as the specification allows. Denials answer JSON with the reason and up to twenty \fBdetails\fR naming the offending path.
.PP
