.SH "maintenance"
.PP
Present means the maintenance gate is available; \fBenabled\fR is the state at start and the runtime toggle (\fBPOST /v1/maintenance\fR, \fBxproxyctl maintenance on|off\fR) overrides it and survives reloads. While it is on, every request is answered with \fBstatus\fR and \fBRetry\-After\fR except an allowlisted client and a route with \fBmaintenance: false\fR (health and status endpoints). The gate runs right after routing, before authentication, rate limits and filters.
.PP
.TS
