.SH "sandbox"
.PP
In\-process hardening applied once the listeners, log files, state files and the management socket are open (docs/HARDENING.md section 1a, docs/HARDENING_MACOS.md on macOS). On by default; \fBGET /v1/sandbox\fR and \fBxproxyctl sandbox\fR show what was applied. The Landlock rules are derived from the configuration: the directory of every configured file is readable, the log, state, history, capture and certificate directories are writable, and nothing else is reachable. A reload that names a file outside those directories is refused with a message to restart.
.PP
.TS
